IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-types`
IMPORT `eia-dates`
IMPORT `eia-supply`
IMPORT `eia-disputes`
IMPORT `eia-enforcement`
IMPORT `eia-goal`

-- Electricity Industry Act 2010 — THE ENCODER'S TESTS.
--
-- Expected values are worked by hand from the Act's text and the calendar
-- (Labour Day 26 October 2026).

§ `Tests`

mat MEANS LIST Date 10 7 2026, Date 25 6 2027

§§ `The supply obligation (ss 105-107)`

GIVEN applies IS A BOOLEAN, ended IS A BOOLEAN, reason IS A `Reason supply ceased`, continuing IS A BOOLEAN, resumed IS A BOOLEAN, knowing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Supply facts`
supply applies ended reason continuing resumed knowing MEANS `Supply facts` OF applies, FALSE, ended, FALSE, reason, continuing, resumed, knowing

#ASSERT `the supply obligation continues` (supply TRUE FALSE `supply has not ceased` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation continues` (supply FALSE FALSE `supply has not ceased` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation continues` (supply TRUE TRUE `supply has not ceased` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation continues` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, `supply has not ceased`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation continues` (`Supply facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, `supply has not ceased`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `the supply obligation is suspended` (supply TRUE FALSE `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the supply obligation is suspended` (supply TRUE FALSE `(c) non-payment of money due for the place` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation is suspended` (supply TRUE FALSE `(b) safety, maintenance or upgrading` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the supply obligation is suspended` (supply TRUE FALSE `another reason` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (supply TRUE FALSE `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control` FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (supply TRUE FALSE `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control` FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (supply TRUE FALSE `(b) safety, maintenance or upgrading` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (supply TRUE FALSE `(b) safety, maintenance or upgrading` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (supply TRUE FALSE `another reason` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the distributor commits the s 105(4) offence` (supply TRUE TRUE `another reason` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the most fine for the s 105(4) offence, days continuing` 10 EQUALS 20000
-- Changed after the independent pass (fork F1): 6 months from 17 October
-- end on 16 April, so supply may begin on 17 April 2027; from 31 August,
-- the period ends at the close of 28 February, so 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT `the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` (Date 16 10 2026) EQUALS Date 17 4 2027
#ASSERT `the earliest day for alternative supply after notice on` (Date 31 8 2026) EQUALS Date 1 3 2027
-- s 80(3)(b)(i) (added after the independent pass): without the court being
-- satisfied of a commercial gain, the $10 million applies.
#ASSERT `the most Part 3 pecuniary penalty for` (`Part 3 contravener` OF FALSE, JUST 8000000, 0, FALSE) EQUALS 10000000
-- Regression: 1 January 2023 was a Sunday, so 4 January was a working day.
#ASSERT `is a working day` (Date 4 1 2023) `, Matariki days` mat
#ASSERT NOT `is a working day` (Date 3 1 2023) `, Matariki days` mat

§§ `Disputes (ss 95-96)`

#ASSERT `a complaint may be made about` `a retailer` `, by a scheme member` FALSE
#ASSERT `a complaint may be made about` `Transpower, other than as system operator` `, by a scheme member` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a complaint may be made about` `Transpower as system operator` `, by a scheme member` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `a complaint may be made about` `a distributor` `, by a scheme member` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `a complaint may be made about` `another industry participant` `, by a scheme member` FALSE

GIVEN k IS A `Kind of participant`, classExempt IS A BOOLEAN, gazetted IS A BOOLEAN, member IS A BOOLEAN, knowing IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Scheme facts`
scheme k classExempt gazetted member knowing MEANS `Scheme facts` OF k, classExempt, gazetted, member, knowing

#ASSERT `must be a member of the dispute resolution scheme` (scheme `a distributor` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `must be a member of the dispute resolution scheme` (scheme `a distributor` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `must be a member of the dispute resolution scheme` (scheme `a retailer` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `must be a member of the dispute resolution scheme` (scheme `another industry participant` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the most fine for not joining the scheme` (scheme `a retailer` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS 100000
#ASSERT `the most fine for not joining the scheme` (scheme `a retailer` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the most fine for not joining the scheme` (scheme `a retailer` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 0

§§ `Enforcement (ss 52, 54, 66, 80)`

GIVEN occurred IS A DATE, discovered IS A DATE, already IS A BOOLEAN, continued IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Code breach`
breach occurred discovered already continued MEANS `Code breach` OF occurred, discovered, Date 16 10 2026, already, continued

#ASSERT `the Authority may act on the breach` (breach (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 16 10 2023) FALSE 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the Authority may act on the breach` (breach (Date 1 1 2023) (Date 15 10 2023) FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `the Authority may act on the breach` (breach (Date 16 10 2016) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE 0)
#ASSERT NOT `the Authority may act on the breach` (breach (Date 15 10 2016) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE 0)
#ASSERT `the Authority may act on the breach` (breach (Date 1 1 2010) (Date 1 1 2011) TRUE 0)
#ASSERT `the most pecuniary penalty for the Code breach` (breach (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE 5) EQUALS 2050000
#ASSERT `the most Part 3 pecuniary penalty for` (`Part 3 contravener` OF TRUE, NOTHING, 0, TRUE) EQUALS 500000
#ASSERT `the most Part 3 pecuniary penalty for` (`Part 3 contravener` OF FALSE, JUST 5000000, 0, TRUE) EQUALS 15000000
#ASSERT `the most Part 3 pecuniary penalty for` (`Part 3 contravener` OF FALSE, NOTHING, 50000000, TRUE) EQUALS 10000000
#ASSERT `the most Part 3 pecuniary penalty for` (`Part 3 contravener` OF FALSE, NOTHING, 200000000, TRUE) EQUALS 20000000
#ASSERT `the last day to appeal a decision of` (Date 16 10 2026) `, Matariki days` mat EQUALS Date 16 11 2026

§§ `The top-level goal`

#ASSERT `the distributor position for` (supply TRUE FALSE `(a) circumstances beyond the distributor's control` TRUE FALSE FALSE) `, scheme` (scheme `a distributor` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `, breach` (breach (Date 1 1 2025) (Date 1 1 2025) FALSE 5) EQUALS `Distributor position` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 2050000
